th('THM-G001','PAPER-G001','Equation (4), pp.500–501','published lemma independently reconstructed','For finite Fq, nontrivial multiplicative χ:Fq*→C* and nontrivial additive ψ:Fq→C*, G=Σx≠0 χ(x)ψ(x) satisfies |G|²=q.','Source inspected and finite-sum proof independently reconstructed; no issue found.',hypotheses=['Both characters nontrivial.','Characters have finite image, hence unit magnitude.'],proof='Substitute x=uy in |G|²; the inner additive sum over y≠0 is q−1 for u=1 and −1 otherwise. Multiplicative orthogonality gives q.')
th('THM-G002','PAPER-G002','Theorem(1.6), p.276; (1.15), p.279','published theorem','For X0 smooth projective over Fq and ℓ≠char Fq, det(tI−F | H^i_et(X0×Fq Fqbar,Qℓ)) has coefficients in Z independent of ℓ; each complex conjugate α of every root satisfies |α|=q^(i/2). F is geometric Frobenius.','Exact theorem and selected dependency architecture inspected; whole proof not independently audited.')
th('THM-G003','PAPER-G002','Theorem(3.2), pp.283–285','published theorem','Let U0⊂P1/Fq be the complement of finitely many closed points, F0 a lisse Qℓ-sheaf, β∈Z. Assume a perfect alternating pairing F0⊗F0→Qℓ(−β); the geometric monodromy image is open in the corresponding symplectic group; and det(1−tFx|F0,x)∈Q[t] for every closed x. Then F0 is pointwise pure of weight β.','Statement and positivity/pole argument inspected; underlying cohomology and invariant-theory results not independently proved.',hypotheses=['ℓ≠char Fq.','Geometric monodromy, not merely arithmetic self-duality.','Rational local characteristic polynomials for every closed point.'])
th('THM-G004','PAPER-G002','Lemma(7.1), pp.298–300; (7.3), p.301','published amplification step','For middle eigenvalue α on a smooth projective absolutely irreducible d-dimensional variety, a dimension-independent q^(d/2±1/2) estimate on even-dimensional cartesian powers gives q^(d/2−1/(2k))≤|α|≤q^(d/2+1/(2k)) and hence |α|=q^(d/2).','Elementary power/Künneth inference checked; geometric derivation of weak estimate not fully audited.')
th('THM-G005','PAPER-G003','Theorem(3.3.1), p.204; conventions(0.1)–(0.2), p.144','published theorem','For f:X→Y between separated noetherian algebraic spaces of finite type over Z with fixed ℓ invertible, and constructible Qℓbar-sheaf F mixed of weights ≤n, R^i f! F is mixed of weights ≤n+i.','Original statement and reduction architecture inspected; full proof not audited.')
th('THM-G006','PAPER-G003','Corollaries(3.3.4)–(3.3.6), p.206','published theorem','Over Fq, Hc^i(X,F) has weights ≤n+i for F mixed of weights ≤n. On smooth X0 and lisse F0 of weights ≥n, H^i has weights ≥n+i. For F0 lisse pure weight n, im(Hc^i→H^i) is pure weight n+i.','Hypotheses and use of opposite duality bounds inspected; no whole-proof audit.')
th('THM-G007','PAPER-G003','Corollary(3.3.9), p.207','published theorem','For X0 smooth proper over Fq and ℓ≠char Fq, the characteristic polynomial of geometric Frobenius on H^i_et(X,Qℓ) is integral and ℓ-independent; all complex eigenvalue conjugates have magnitude q^(i/2).','Source statement inspected; extension proper vs projective checked.')
th('THM-G008','PAPER-G003','Corollary(2.2.10), p.196; context(2.1.9), p.191','published theorem','For X0/Fq smooth curve and F0 lisse iota-pure of weight β, every Frobenius eigenvalue α on Hc^1(X,F) satisfies wq(α)<β+2, wq(α)=2log_q|iota(α)|.','Statement/image and Hadamard–de la Vallée-Poussin connection inspected; complete representation-theoretic proof not audited.')
th('THM-G009','PAPER-G003','Lemma(3.2.4)(k), p.197 through proof(3.2.15), p.204','published theorem','For every k≥0, smooth U0/Fq and F0 lisse iota-pure weight0, eigenvalues α on Hc^1(U,F) satisfy wq(α)≤1+2^(−k). Passing to the limit supplies the optimal upper weight bound; duality then yields curve purity in the proper intermediate-extension statement.','Exact statement and product-iteration architecture inspected; all local calculations not independently audited.')
th('THM-G010',None,'frontiers/geometry_round2.md §3','independently proved auxiliary obstruction','Z*(t)=(1−5t+5t²)/((1−t)(1−5t)) has integral Taylor coefficients, nonnegative integer Euler exponents in every degree, genus-one reciprocal functional equation, and a finite alternating-duality trace model, but numerator eigenvalues (5±sqrt5)/2 have magnitudes unequal to sqrt5.','Explicit all-degree labeled-graph proof reconstructed; parent independently checked injection, exact periods and recurrence. No literature novelty claim.',proof_file='frontiers/geometry_round2.md',test_file='experiments/code/geometry_round2_exact.py',status='established auxiliary negative result; not a counterexample to any actual curve theorem or classical RH')
th('THM-G011',None,'frontiers/geometry_round2.md §3, genuine lisse-sheaf test','independently reconstructed hypothesis-deletion example','For ℓ≠5, geometric Frobenius A=[[2,1],[1,3]] defines a continuous Gal(F5bar/F5) representation pulled back to A1/F5. It has a perfect alternating pairing to Qℓ(−1) and rational local characteristic polynomials but is not pure of weight1; geometric monodromy is trivial. L(A1,V^⊗2k,t)=det(1−5t A^⊗2k)^−1.','Parent independently checked continuity, geometric/arithmetic Frobenius convention and pole formula; no issue found.',source_theorems=['THM-G003'],role='Tests deletion of the open-geometric-monodromy hypothesis; not a contradiction to Deligne.')
th('THM-G012',None,'frontiers/geometry_round2.md §4','elementary amplification lemma','If q>1, α≠0, and for arbitrarily large k, q^(kw/2−Ck)≤|α|^k≤q^(kw/2+Ck) with Ck=o(k), then |α|=q^(w/2).','Independent logarithm/division proof; abstraction of DeligneI(7.3), no novelty claim.',source_theorems=['THM-G004'])
th('THM-G013',None,'frontiers/geometry_round2.md §9','derived sufficient-condition lemma pending independent review','For affine U0⊂P1/Fq and lisse F0 with perfect alternating pairing to Qℓ(−β) and rational local characteristic polynomials, suppose for arbitrarily large k all Frobenius eigenvalues on (V^⊗2k)_geometric-monodromy are algebraic and every conjugate has magnitude ≤q^(kβ+Ck), Ck≥0, Ck=o(k). Then F0 is pointwise pure weightβ.','Proof reconstruction supplied; separate review of coefficient-field descent and local/global radius comparison pending. Do not assign literature novelty.',source_theorems=['THM-G003','THM-G012'],proof_file='frontiers/geometry_round2.md',status='derived lemma under review')
